{"id":"Q02","requested_parts":["Objective filtering and dealing.","When an Objective is chosen and what happens to the rejected card.","Whether Eggs trigger that choice."],"answer":"1. Remove cards requiring more than P players from both Objective decks; separately shuffle and deal each player 1 Corporate and 1 Personal Objective, kept hidden. 2. At the First Encounter, each player immediately chooses 1 of their 2 Objectives; remove the other face down, unseen by anyone. 3. Eggs do not trigger the choice; the first Intruder miniature appearing does, and Eggs are not Intruders.","support":"supported","evidence":"1. “Let P be the actual number of players in this game. Remove from both Objective decks (Corporate and Personal) every card requiring more than P players. Shuffle the two decks separately and deal each player 1 Corporate and 1 Personal Objective card, kept hidden.” 2. “First Encounter: the first time an Intruder miniature (of any type) appears on the board, every player immediately chooses 1 of their 2 Objective cards and removes the other from the game face down (unseen by anyone — players may never look at others' removed Objectives). Then the triggering Encounter is resolved.” 3. “Eggs are not Intruders and do not trigger this.”"},
