{"id":"Q61","requested_parts":["What happens to the One Use Only Item card after its Action is used."],"answer":"1. Discard the One Use Only Item after its effect, in addition to paying its Action-card cost and showing it.","support":"supported","evidence":"“One Use Only means discard that Item after its effect, in addition to paying its Action-card cost.” “Any Item used must be shown to all players.”"},
{"id":"Q62","requested_parts":["Where a launched Escape Pod Character counts as having arrived for Character-arrival rules.","Whether that establishes that the ship itself reached Earth."],"answer":"1. The occupants count as having arrived on Earth. 2. This only establishes the Escape Pod occupants' arrival; the summary does not say the ship itself reached Earth. That is a separate destination/ship outcome.","support":"supported","evidence":"1. “Launch immediately: after boarding you may launch. Remove the Pod token and its occupants' miniatures from the game; they stop participating and count as arriving on Earth. They still face the final Contamination and Objective checks.” 2. Inference from that rule: it specifically describes the Pod occupants as arriving on Earth and does not establish the ship's destination or arrival; those are handled separately by the Coordinates check, which reveals the Coordinates card and reads the destination selected by the Destination marker."},
{"id":"Q63","requested_parts":["Whether a waiting Escape Pod occupant rolls Noise when Adult bag development calls for it."],"answer":"1. Yes. A waiting Character remains treated as present in the Section for bag-development Noise rolls, and Adult bag development calls for all players to roll in order, skipping Characters in Combat.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Wait after boarding — complete waiting procedure: choosing to wait makes you pass the current turn, while you remain treated as present in the Section for bag-development Noise rolls (FAQ Rules 1).” “Adult — return the token to the bag immediately before all players roll for Noise in order (skip Characters in Combat). An Encounter from those rolls may draw that same Adult token (FAQ Rules 7).”"},
{"id":"Q64","requested_parts":["Whether an already-waiting occupant may launch, wait, or exit when a Malfunction is placed in the Section.","What the Malfunction prevents."],"answer":"1. Yes. You retain the choices to wait, launch, or exit. 2. The Malfunction blocks only new Pod entry.","support":"supported","evidence":"“While waiting, apply all three contingencies: ... if a Malfunction appears, your normal wait/launch/exit choices remain available and only new entry is blocked.” “A Malfunction appears in the Section | You may still wait, launch or exit; the marker blocks only new Pod entry (FAQ Rules 3).”"},
{"id":"Q65","requested_parts":["Number of Intruder Attacks when Escaping several Intruders.","The order of attacks for different sizes."],"answer":"1. Resolve one separate Intruder Attack per Intruder in the Room. 2. Start with the largest, in order: Queen, Breeder, Adult, Larva.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Character Escape: to leave a Room containing Intruders, perform a Movement Action (cost 1) to a neighboring Room (explored or unexplored). BEFORE moving, resolve an Intruder Attack — one separate Attack per Intruder in the Room, starting with the larger ones (Queen, Breeder, Adult, Larva; FAQ Rules 5).”"},
{"id":"Q66","requested_parts":["Whether an Event instructed to remove itself is removed if its other effect cannot resolve."],"answer":"1. Yes. Remove it from the game even when its other effect cannot be resolved.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Remove an Event that says to remove itself even when its other effect cannot resolve (Rules 6).”"},
{"id":"Q67","requested_parts":["When the Adult bag-development token returns relative to Noise rolls.","Whether the Encounter triggered by those Noise rolls can draw the same Adult token."],"answer":"1. Return the drawn Adult token to the bag immediately before all players roll Noise in order, skipping Characters in Combat. 2. Yes. An Encounter caused by those rolls may draw that same Adult token.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Adult — return the token to the bag immediately before all players roll for Noise in order (skip Characters in Combat). An Encounter from those rolls may draw that same Adult token (FAQ Rules 7).”"},
{"id":"Q68","requested_parts":["What happens when a retreating Intruder meets a Closed Door normally.","How The Way of Moving changes this for affected Intruders other than Breeders and the Queen."],"answer":"1. Normally it destroys the Closed Door and stays in place. 2. For an Intruder affected by The Way of Moving, other than a Breeder or Queen, it instead does nothing at the Door; the Intruder does not pass through it or destroy it.","support":"supported","evidence":"“A retreating Intruder meeting a Closed Door destroys it and stays. With The Way of Moving Weakness, an affected Intruder other than a Breeder or Queen instead does nothing at that Door (Rules 8).”"},
{"id":"Q69","requested_parts":["Whether the Hand Serious Wound raises Basic Shoot's Action cost and why."],"answer":"1. No. Basic Shoot is a Basic Action, not an Item Action, so the Hand Serious Wound does not increase its cost.","support":"supported","evidence":"“The Hand Serious Wound does not increase Basic Shoot cost because Shoot is a Basic Action, not an Item Action (Rules 9; Items 7).”"},
{"id":"Q70","requested_parts":["How much extra Injury Vulnerability to Fire adds per damage instance.","Total Injuries from a Flamethrower double-crosshair hit with that Weakness."],"answer":"1. It adds 1 Injury per damage instance, rather than per individual Injury. 2. A Flamethrower double-crosshair result causes 3 Injuries: the usual 2 plus 1 additional Injury for that damage instance.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Vulnerability to Fire gives 1 additional Injury per damage instance (x + 1), rather than per individual Injury. A Flamethrower double-crosshair hit therefore deals 3 Injuries; Fire in the Nest destroys 2 Eggs per Fire Damage step with this Weakness (Rules 11; Rooms 7).” Inference for part 2: the cited rule explicitly gives 3 Injuries for this hit, which is the double-crosshair result plus one extra injury."}
