{"id":"Q71","requested_parts":["What happens to the attacking Larva when the target already has a Larva.","What happens to the existing Larva and the Character."],"answer":"1. The attacking Larva disappears. 2. The existing Larva stays on the Character; the Character gains only the new Contamination card, and this Larva attack does not automatically kill them. The Contamination card goes on top of the Character's Action discard pile.","support":"supported","evidence":"1. “If the target already has a Larva, the attacking Larva disappears, the existing one stays, and the Character only gains the Contamination card; this attack does not automatically kill them (FAQ Rules 12).” 2. The same Infest rule states the existing Larva stays, the Character gains the Contamination card, and the attack does not automatically kill them. “When a Character ‘gets a Contamination card,’ draw it from the Contamination deck and place it on top of their Action discard pile.”"},
{"id":"Q72","requested_parts":["Whether the sleeper takes Fire wounds from Fire in the Hibernatorium.","What can still kill the sleeper."],"answer":"1. No. A sleeper takes no later Fire wounds in the Hibernatorium. 2. Ship destruction and endgame survival checks can still kill them: for example, 2 or 3 Damaged Engines explode the ship and kill hibernating Characters; a non-Earth destination kills hibernating Characters (except a sleeper with Quarantine when the destination is Mars); and surviving Characters still undergo the Contamination check.","support":"supported","evidence":"1. “A sleeper takes no later Fire wounds in the Hibernatorium, though ship destruction and the endgame survival checks still matter (Rules 13).” 2. “2 or 3 Damaged Engines make the ship explode. EVERYTHING aboard dies, including hibernating Characters and Intruders.” “Non-Earth kills hibernating Characters, while the ship is not destroyed and Intruders remain alive. A sleeper with the Quarantine Objective survives if the destination is Mars.” The contamination check applies “for every surviving Character, including launched Pod passengers”; any Contamination card among the four drawn “kills you, whether Infected or not.”"},
{"id":"Q73","requested_parts":["Whether Coolant Leak may start Self-Destruct while a Character is hibernating.","How that differs from a Character starting it."],"answer":"1. Yes, Coolant Leak can start Self-Destruct despite sleepers, but only if the Generator has a Malfunction. 2. A Character cannot start Self-Destruct while anyone is hibernating; the Event is the stated exception.","support":"supported","evidence":"1. “Coolant Leak exception (illustrated Event, manual p.10): after its normal Intruder movement, start Self-Destruct if the Generator has a Malfunction.” “Characters cannot start Self-Destruct while any Character is hibernating; the Coolant Leak Event can start it despite sleepers (FAQ Rules 14).” 2. The same rule says: “Characters cannot start Self-Destruct while any Character is hibernating; the Coolant Leak Event can start it despite sleepers (FAQ Rules 14).”"},
{"id":"Q74","requested_parts":["Where discarded or dead Intruder tokens go.","Whether they may be reused."],"answer":"1. Discarded/dead Intruder tokens return to the unused token pool. 2. Yes; they remain reusable and are not removed permanently.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Discarded/dead Intruder tokens return to the unused token pool and remain reusable; they are not removed permanently (Rules 19).”"},
{"id":"Q75","requested_parts":["Whether Fire markers can be placed in unexplored Rooms.","Whether Malfunction markers can be placed in unexplored Rooms."],"answer":"1. Yes. Fire markers can be placed in unexplored Rooms. 2. No. Malfunction markers cannot be placed in unexplored Rooms.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Malfunction markers cannot be placed in unexplored Rooms, whereas Fire markers can (FAQ Rules 22).”"},
{"id":"Q76","requested_parts":["What Wounds remain after two Light Wounds are received while already at two Light Wounds."],"answer":"1. After the third Light Wound clears the Light Wound track and causes 1 Serious Wound, the fourth Light Wound leaves 1 Light Wound. The Character therefore has 1 Serious Wound and 1 Light Wound.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Two Light Wounds suffered while already at 2 Light Wounds become 1 Serious Wound plus 1 remaining Light Wound (Rules 23).”"},
{"id":"Q77","requested_parts":["What happens to Heavy Objects when a Character dies in standard play.","What happens to their Item cards."],"answer":"1. Their Heavy Objects are dropped in the Room. The Character's miniature is removed and a Character Corpse token is placed in that Room as a Character Corpse Object. 2. Item cards disappear from the game.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Death: a Character with 3 Serious Wounds dies instantly upon suffering ANY additional Wound (Light or Serious). Remove the miniature, place a Character Corpse token in the Room (now a Character Corpse Object), and drop all their Heavy Objects there.” “On death in standard play, Heavy Objects drop in the Room, while Item cards disappear from the game (Rules 24).”"},
{"id":"Q78","requested_parts":["Whether reaching a later yellow Self-Destruct space unlocks Pods again after they were re-Locked following the first yellow space."],"answer":"1. No. Pods unlock automatically only when the Self-Destruct marker first reaches a yellow space; although they may be re-Locked, subsequent yellow spaces do not unlock them again.","support":"supported","evidence":"“At the first yellow space: the sequence can no longer be aborted, and all Escape Pods unlock instantly. They can be re-Locked; subsequent yellow spaces do not unlock them again (FAQ Rules 25).”"},
{"id":"Q79","requested_parts":["Whether ship destruction fulfills kill-the-Queen or destroy-the-Nest Objectives.","Whether this alone makes the Character a winner."],"answer":"1. Yes. Destruction of the ship fulfills the Objective requirements to kill the Queen or destroy the Nest. 2. No. Your Character must still survive and fulfill their Objective; surviving alone is insufficient.","support":"supported","evidence":"1. “Destruction of the ship fulfills kill-Queen/destroy-Nest requirements; your Character must still survive and fulfill their Objective (Rules 26).” 2. “Regardless of Objective, your Character must survive (Escape Pod or hibernation).” “Objectives: each still-living Character reveals their chosen Objective and wins only if all requirements are fulfilled. Merely surviving is insufficient.”"},
{"id":"Q80","requested_parts":["Whether a player may intentionally perform a Trade with no intention of exchange.","What happens if genuine negotiations end with no trade."],"answer":"1. No. Empty Actions that cause no meaningful game-state change are disallowed, including starting Trade with no intention of exchanging anything. 2. Honest negotiations may end without a trade; that is allowed.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Empty Actions that make no meaningful game-state change should be disallowed, including starting Trade with no intention of exchange. Honest negotiations may end with no trade. Any Characters in the Room can trade with each other, including pairs who did not initiate/pay (Actions 1–2).”"}
]`;
