{"id":"Q91","requested_parts":["Whether an empty hand after two Actions automatically passes the player.","What timing consequences Fire or Bleeding may have."],"answer":"1. No. Completing two Actions with an empty hand ends that round but does not automatically pass; apply that round's end effects, wait until the player's next round, and declare Pass then. 2. That passing round may cause another Fire or Bleeding effect; Fire applies at the end of the passing round after the Pass is declared.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Empty-hand sequence: completing 2 Actions with an empty hand ends that round, but does not automatically pass you. Apply the round's end effects, then wait for your next round; declare Pass then. That passing round can incur another Fire or Bleeding effect (Actions 18). Fire applies at the end of your passing round, after you declare Pass.”"},
{"id":"Q92","requested_parts":["Whether multiple Infected cards scanned by Rest can kill when no Larva was on the Character's board before Rest.","When Rest can be fatal."],"answer":"1. No. If there was no Larva before Rest, multiple Infected cards do not kill you from that scan; place just 1 Larva. 2. Rest can be fatal if a Larva was already on the Character board before the Action: an ordinary Infected scan with a Larva already present kills the Character.","support":"supported","evidence":"1. “Rest with no Larva before the Action cannot kill you merely because several scanned cards are Infected: place just 1 Larva.” 2. “Rest can be fatal if a Larva was already on the board before it (Actions 19).” The general ordinary-scan rule states: “If an ordinary Scan shows INFECTED (follow its specific Action procedure; Surgery removes Infected cards/Larva, while Rest and Alcohol have the FAQ exceptions below): place a Larva miniature on your Character board and do NOT remove that Contamination card. If a Larva is already on your board, your Character dies — and place 1 Creeper in the Room where you died.”"},
{"id":"Q93","requested_parts":["Where to resolve the required Noise roll after throwing a Grenade or Molotov at uncarried Nest Eggs from a neighboring Room."],"answer":"1. Roll Noise in your own Room, where you threw the Grenade or Molotov, not in the Nest.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Throwing a Grenade/Molotov at Nest Eggs from another Room makes you roll Noise in your own Room, not the Nest (Rooms 2, 9).”"},
{"id":"Q94","requested_parts":["Whether Scientist can reveal a Weakness by researching an Object carried outside the Laboratory."],"answer":"1. No. The Object itself must be in the Laboratory to be researched; Scientist's location or use of Intranet does not waive that requirement.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Intranet research still requires the Object itself in the Laboratory, regardless of Scientist's location. Research means Analyse; the Object is retained, including for Objectives (Rooms 3–4).”"},
{"id":"Q95","requested_parts":["Whether Storage Room Action may be used repeatedly at Item Counter zero.","How ordinary Search differs at Item Counter zero."],"answer":"1. Yes. Storage's separate Room Action can be used repeatedly at counter zero, paying its normal cost and following normal Room Action restrictions. 2. Ordinary Search is the Search Action card; each use lowers the Item Counter by 1 and at zero the Room cannot be searched, except for Scout's Scavenging.","support":"supported","evidence":"1. “Storage's Room Action works repeatedly even with its Item Counter at zero, paying the normal cost and obeying normal Room restrictions. Its counter limits only the Search Action card (Rooms 6).” 2. “In other Rooms, each Search lowers the Item Counter by 1; at 0 the Room cannot be searched (exception: Scout's Scavenging).”"},
{"id":"Q96","requested_parts":["Number of Nest Eggs destroyed in each Fire Damage step with Vulnerability to Fire."],"answer":"1. The Nest's Egg pool loses 2 Eggs per Fire Damage step while Vulnerability to Fire is discovered.","support":"supported","evidence":"“Vulnerability to Fire gives 1 additional Injury per damage instance (x + 1), rather than per individual Injury. A Flamethrower double-crosshair hit therefore deals 3 Injuries; Fire in the Nest destroys 2 Eggs per Fire Damage step with this Weakness (Rules 11; Rooms 7).” The Egg rule also states: “For the Nest's Egg pool, Vulnerability to Fire increases this to 2 per step (FAQ Rooms 7).”"},
{"id":"Q97","requested_parts":["Whether an Egg taken from the Intruder board and dropped back into the Nest restores the Nest Egg total for destruction."],"answer":"1. No. Once taken from the Intruder board and dropped in the Nest Room, it is a normal Heavy Object and does not restore the Nest's Egg total or hit points.","support":"supported","evidence":"“An Egg taken from the Intruder board and dropped back in the Nest is a normal Heavy Object and does not restore the Nest's Egg total/hit points (Rooms 2, 9).”"},
